# All times are LOCAL (Europe/Bucharest). Do not add CRON_TZ - Debian's cron
# does not implement it. It parses as a plain environment assignment, is
# silently ignored for scheduling, and every job below then runs at the stated
# time in local terms anyway. Tried on 2026-08-20, reverted 2026-08-21 after it
# moved the whole window three hours early and put restic ahead of its sources.
#
# The Oracle VPS, the k8s cluster and Nextcloud AIO all schedule in UTC. In
# summer their jobs land at 02:40-03:02 local, just before this window. In
# winter they drop an hour to 01:40-02:02 while these stay put, so the SAS pool
# wakes twice a night instead of once. That is accepted: the ordering that
# matters still holds - every source still writes before restic reads at 03:10 -
# and the alternative is running eight systemd timers to gain one spin-up.
#
# Order matters: every source writes before restic reads at 03:10.

# REDACTED - the weekly Synology push time reveals the NAS wake window, which
# this repo deliberately does not publish. Real line is in
# /root/PRIVATE-NOTES.md on pve (restic backs it up). Restoring from this file
# alone therefore leaves the weekly leg unscheduled - add it back.
# <min> <hr> * * <day> /root/scripts/weekly-push-to-synology.sh

# --- nightly backup window ---
55 2 * * *  /usr/bin/vzdump 101 --mode snapshot --compress zstd --storage sas-backups --prune-backups keep-last=1 >> /var/log/vzdump-cron.log 2>&1
1 3 * * *   /root/scripts/garage-meta-nightly-copy.sh >> /var/log/garage-meta-copy.log 2>&1
3 3 * * *   /root/scripts/etcd-snapshot.sh >> /var/log/etcd-snapshot.log 2>&1
5 3 * * *   /root/scripts/zfs-snapshot-backups.sh >> /var/log/zfs-snapshot.log 2>&1
10 3 * * *  /root/scripts/restic-push-oracle.sh >> /var/log/restic-push.log 2>&1
20 3 * * *  /root/scripts/sas-health-check.sh >> /var/log/sas-health.log 2>&1
25 3 * * *  /root/scripts/spindown-drift-check.sh >> /var/log/spindown-drift.log 2>&1

# --- monthly ---
0 5 1 * *   /root/scripts/restic-restore-drill.sh >> /var/log/restic-restore-drill.log 2>&1

# --- every 5 minutes ---
*/5 * * * * /root/scripts/heartbeat-ping.sh >> /var/log/heartbeat-ping.log 2>&1
